claimed: intent-static-embeddings — a classifier with no external gateway at request time. Rather than downloading model2vec, do what model2vec DOES: distil a static table from the teacher we already have -- embed a vocabulary once, offline, store the vectors, and at request time tokenize, look up and pool. Three consequences worth the lane: the table inherits the semantics our probe already works with, no download and no foreign tokenizer are needed, and the result is pure array arithmetic that crosses to JS and Native where an ONNX runtime could not. Zipf-style weighting as model2vec applies it. The vocabulary comes from the TRAINING half only, so out-of-vocabulary words in the test half are a measured cost rather than a leak. The number that matters is how much is lost against the teacher: the probe is 88.3% on live vectors and chargrams are 60% with no network, and this is the candidate that could sit near the top of that range while needing nothing at all.
